  "editorial": {
    "status": "working-edition",
    "notes": "The complete threefold Agnus Dei printed for Feria V in Cena Domini: every invocation ends miserere nobis. The kiss of peace and Domine Iesu Christe, qui dixisti are omitted. These omissions do not suppress Pax Domini or the two following Communion prayers. The priestly recitation is audible at low Mass and quiet at sung Mass; the sung Ordinary performance is separately represented (RG 511 i, 513 e, 514; DMS 25 b, 26, 31 c).",
    "source": {
      "method": "Read separately from the Benziger 1962 Editio iuxta typicam, p. 162, no. 28, and the separately set Vatican 1962 Missal, p. 159, no. 28. Both print all three complete invocations; the witnesses agree in wording and punctuation. Ordinary line wrapping is joined.",
